      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We reported a rare case of a 53-year-old man who experienced acute myocardial infarction due to simultaneous occlusion in the right coronary artery and the left anterior descending coronary artery. He also experienced thromboembolisms on several occasions. So anticoagulant therapy is necessary for patients with exceedingly poor LV function."},
